course: dictionary
lesson: 2522
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and decline is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context. «The population of bees is declining» is about numbers, so decline means getting smaller.
explain: «Ayesha politely declined the invitation to the party.» Here decline means to say no politely. Ask yourself what fits. If you try "got smaller" instead, the sentence makes no sense, so that meaning is wrong.
explain: Decline can also be a noun, a name for a fall, as in «a sharp decline in numbers». The phrase «in decline» means getting worse or fewer. When you meet decline, check the clues in the sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Decline has three main meanings: to say no politely, to get smaller or worse, and a fall in amount.
fact: «Decline an invitation» means to politely say no to it.
fact: «Decline in numbers» means the numbers are getting smaller.
fact: A decline is a fall: on a graph, a line going down shows a decline.
fact: A debit card can be declined at the till if there is not enough money in the account.
exercise: «Ayesha politely declined the invitation to the party.» What does declined mean here? | *To say no politely | To feel very happy | To get smaller and fewer | To fall down a hill
exercise: «The population of bees is declining.» What does declining mean here? | Being kept by a beekeeper | *Getting smaller in number | Flying to a new place | Buzzing louder every day
exercise: Why was the snack declined at the till when the account had only £3 in it? | *The account had too little money for the snack | The snack was too small | The card was too old | The shop was closed
test: «Leaders do not have to take part in debates; when one declines, a channel may show an empty podium.» What does declines mean? | Falls over | *Says no to taking part | Sings loudly | Grows bigger and stronger
test: Which sentence uses decline as a noun, meaning a fall? | *The bees show a sharp decline. | The bees are declining fast. | He will decline the cake. | We must decline the offer.
exam: «If a prey animal disappears, the predators must find other food, move away or decline.» What does decline mean here? | To say no politely | *To get smaller or worse | To fall asleep | To go up and up
